## `ledgerkit.models`

`models.py` holds plain dataclasses only — no parsing or reporting
logic lives there (journal-parsing@v1#journal-parsing-010; the module
has zero imports from `parser.py`).

### `Amount`

Fields: `quantity: Decimal`, `commodity: str`, `raw: Optional[str] =
None`. `raw` is excluded from `repr`/`__eq__` comparison, so two
`Amount`s with the same quantity and commodity compare equal
regardless of how each was originally written in source text
(journal-parsing@v1#journal-parsing-010). `Amount` carries a method,
`display(style)`, which delegates directly to the given style object's
own `format(quantity)` method (see `ledgerkit.commodity_style` below).

A posting in ledgerkit's current data model can reference at most one
commodity in its main amount — there is no `MixedAmount` concept
(tags@v1#tags-009).

### `BalanceAssertion`

Fields: `amount: Amount`, `inclusive: bool = False`, `sole_commodity:
bool = False`. These two independent booleans together cover all four
of hledger's balance-assertion markers (`=`, `==`, `=*`, `==*`):
`inclusive` selects whether subaccounts are summed in (the `*`
variants), and `sole_commodity` selects whether every other commodity
present in that account must be exactly zero (the `==` variants)
(checks@v1#checks-006).

### `SourceSpan`

Fields: `file: str`, `start_line: int`, `end_line: int`; both line
numbers are 1-indexed and inclusive (journal-parsing@v1#journal-parsing-010).

### `Posting`

Fields include `account: str`, `amount: Optional[Amount] = None`,
`balance_assertion: Optional[BalanceAssertion] = None`, `cost_raw:
Optional[str] = None`, `source_line: Optional[int] = None`, `inferred:
bool = False`, `inline_comment: Optional[str] = None`, `tags:
list[tuple[str, str]]`, `date_override: Optional[date] = None`,
`date2_override: Optional[date] = None`
(journal-parsing@v1#journal-parsing-010,
journal-parsing@v1#journal-parsing-005). `inline_comment` is excluded
from equality comparison; `date_override`/`date2_override` are
deliberately *included* in equality comparison, per an in-model
comment explaining that they change parsing-visible state, not merely
provenance (journal-parsing@v1#journal-parsing-010).

`Posting.date_override`/`date2_override` are set only from the first
occurrence of a `date`/`date2` comment tag on that posting's own
parsed tags — never from the transaction's own tags, and a
`date`/`date2` tag written in a transaction-level comment has no
override effect at all (journal-parsing@v1#journal-parsing-010,
tags@v1#tags-008). An unparseable date value in such a tag is a hard
error, raised immediately in strict mode or collected (with the
override left unset) in lenient mode
(journal-parsing@v1#journal-parsing-010).

### `Transaction`

Fields include `date: date`, `description: str`, `date2: Optional[date]
= None`, `postings: list[Posting]`, `cleared: bool = False`, `pending:
bool = False`, `code: str = ""`, `comment: str = ""`, `source_line:
Optional[int] = None`, `source_span: Optional[SourceSpan] = None`,
`raw_text: Optional[str] = None`, `inline_comment: Optional[str] =
None`, `tags: list[tuple[str, str]]`
(journal-parsing@v1#journal-parsing-010). There is deliberately no
`date_override`-equivalent field at the transaction level — this is an
explicit design choice, not an oversight
(journal-parsing@v1#journal-parsing-010, tags@v1#tags-008).

### `PriceDirective`

Fields: `date: date`, `commodity: str`, `price: Amount`
(journal-parsing@v1#journal-parsing-010).

### `Journal`

A container with fields including `transactions: list[Transaction]`,
`prices: list[PriceDirective]`, `declared_accounts: list[str]`,
`declared_commodities: list[str]`, `declared_payees: list[str]`,
`declared_tags: list[str]`, `declared_account_tags: dict[str,
list[tuple[str, str]]]`, `declared_commodity_tags: dict[str,
list[tuple[str, str]]]`, `source_file: Optional[str]`,
`included_files: int`
(journal-parsing@v1#journal-parsing-010, loader@v1#loader-006,
loader@v1#loader-008, tags@v1#tags-001). `declared_account_tags` and
`declared_commodity_tags` are keyed by the exact declared account
path / commodity symbol — not pre-expanded for inheritance
(tags@v1#tags-004).

`Journal` also exposes convenience report methods (`balance`,
`register`, `accounts`, `stats`, `to_dataframe`, `commodity_styles`)
that lazily delegate into `ledgerkit.reports`,
`ledgerkit.commodity_style`, and `ledgerkit.query`
(journal-parsing@v1#journal-parsing-010). `Journal.commodity_styles`
is documented further under `ledgerkit.commodity_style` below.

### `Journal.commodity_styles` resolution order

`Journal.commodity_styles` resolves one `CommodityStyle` per commodity
symbol using a three-pass priority scheme, highest priority last in
code but documented as winning overall: (1) the first posting amount
seen for that commodity, in transaction/posting order; (2) failing
that, the first price-directive amount for that commodity; (3) an
explicit `commodity` directive's own sample amount for that symbol,
which unconditionally overwrites whatever either earlier pass set
(commodity-styling@v1#commodity-styling-005). No test in the permitted
evidence directly exercises this directive-overrides-posting priority
claim; it rests on direct reading of the property's own docstring and
implementation, which were independently confirmed to agree with each
other (commodity-styling@v1#commodity-styling-005).

