## `ledgerkit.writer`

### `transaction_to_text(txn: Transaction) -> str`

Serialises a single `Transaction` to hledger journal-format text. The
returned string is guaranteed to round-trip through `parse_string()`
to an equivalent `Transaction` — same date, flag, description,
postings, amounts, and comments; `source_span`/`raw_text` are excluded
from that guarantee (reports-cli@v1#reports-cli-014). Amount columns
are right-aligned to a shared column computed from the widest account
name among postings that carry an explicit amount, plus a minimum
two-space gap; an elided posting (no amount) is printed as a bare
`"    {account}"` line (reports-cli@v1#reports-cli-014).

### `journal_to_text(journal: Journal) -> str`

Serialises every transaction in `journal.transactions`, separated by
exactly one blank line. It explicitly does **not** serialise
directives (`account`, `commodity`, `payee`, `P`) as of this version —
a caller needing full round-trip fidelity for directive content should
work with the raw source file rather than re-serialising the `Journal`
(reports-cli@v1#reports-cli-014).

